<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Moab</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 BCE – 582 BCE (approx.) · capital Dibon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Moab, a kingdom east of the Dead Sea whose king Mesha recorded his revolt against Israel on the famous Mesha Stele.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Moab took shape in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> on the plateau east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnon">Arnon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zered">Zered</a> gorges. Egyptian texts mention the land in the 13th century BCE, and by the 9th century BCE it was a kingdom with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhiban">Dibon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Moabite kings ruled a land of wheat fields and sheep pastures under the protection of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chemosh">Chemosh</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesha-stele">Mesha Stele</a>, found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhiban">Dhiban</a> in 1868, tells how <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesha">Mesha</a> freed Moab from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab</a>'s dynasty had held it, building towns and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">reservoirs</a>. Its language was close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Moab became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> in the 8th century BCE and later of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>. A Babylonian campaign in 582 BCE ended its independence, and Arab tribes and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nabataean-kingdom">Nabataean Kingdom</a> took over the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/moab.jpg" alt="Moab" width="320" height="382"><figcaption>Image: FinnWikiNo; derivative work by Richardprins... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdoms_around_Israel_830_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 BCE – 582 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dibon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mesha, Kamashaltu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Moabite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Moabite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Moab, Moabites</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-791&amp;focus=moab" aria-label="Moab on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5603 1030 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Moab lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5923 1286L5905 1260M5923 1286L6092 1134M5923 1286L6140 1251"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5905 1260h0M6092 1134h0M6140 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5923 1286h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5923 1286h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-791&amp;focus=moab">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

